{
  "dom_id": "step-q78566",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $3\\times 3$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x=d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{3}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x=A\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ x & =BA\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
